  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is $8x+32y+{y}^{2}=-263-{x}^{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x+32y+{y}^{2} & =-263-{x}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+8x)+({y}^{2}+32y) & =-263 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 16y+{16}^{2}) & =-263+{4}^{2}+{16}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 16y+{16}^{2}) & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+(y+16)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-16))^{2} & ={3}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-4,-16)$ and its radius is $3.$",
